% M8-bits-encoding-T3 continuation (D-0134 section 9): bool2int over a BITS integer. At
% `--bits-above 0` x (0..5) and y (0..9) are on bits, so bool2int(b, x) is posted as its
% two rows with a [Linear] each and justified by Linear's bits `pol`: at the root b's top
% confines x to 0..1 and y = x + 3 to 3..4. Deciding y = 3 fixes x = 0, which pushes b to
% 0 (the x -> b direction, over a bits row), and the two clauses b \/ c and b \/ ~c then
% clash: the trace reaches the page at that conflict, the learned clause sends y to 4, x
% to 1 and b to 1 (the b -> x direction read the other way), and c is left to the search.
var bool: b :: output_var;
var bool: c :: output_var;
var 0..5: x :: output_var;
var 0..9: y :: output_var;
constraint bool2int(b, x);
constraint int_lin_eq([1, -1], [y, x], 3);
constraint bool_clause([b, c], []);
constraint bool_clause([b], [c]);
solve :: int_search([y], input_order, indomain_min, complete) satisfy;
